{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>When you go forth to battle, etc. And you see horse and chariot, etc.</b> — This is a new commandment, which He stated to them now as they were about to enter into wars. The reason for <b>for HaShem your Elohim is the One who goes with you to fight for you against your enemies, to save you</b> — He warns them that their hearts should not fail and they should not fear the enemies, and He says that they should not rely on this through their own might, thinking in their hearts, 'We are mighty and men of valor for battle'; rather, they should turn their hearts back to HaShem and trust in His salvation, and they should consider that it is not by the might of the horse that He desires, nor by the legs of a man is He pleased, for HaShem desires those who fear Him, those who hope for His kindness. And He said 'to fight for you against your enemies,' because He will cause them to fall by the sword before you. And He said 'to save you' — that they themselves will be delivered in battle and not a single man among them will be lost, for it is possible that they might defeat their enemies and yet many of them also die, in the manner of wars. Therefore Joshua cried out when thirty-six men of theirs fell at Ai (Joshua 7:7–9), for in an obligatory war of His it was not fitting that even a hair of their head should fall to the ground, for the battle is HaShem's. Now the priest, who is the one who serves HaShem, warns them in fear of Him and gives them assurance, but the officers speak in the way of the world: 'lest he die in battle' — for by the way of the land, in all wars men die even from among the victorious side. And He commanded concerning these three [categories of men] to return, because his heart is upon his house and his vineyard and upon his wife, and he will flee."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:52:04.095424707Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}